+Following up on House 5 now that we've started treatment. The birds are on amoxicillin in the drinking water — a five-day course — and they're already picking up, so medically that was the right call.
+
+The part I need you on is the eggs. Amoxicillin carries an egg withdrawal: eggs laid during dosing, and for five days after the last dose, can't go into the table-egg supply. The residue can sit above the allowable limit, and it's exactly the sort of thing a retailer or FDA residue screen catches after the fact. So for that whole window, House 5's production has to come off the shell account and stay out of the human food chain — diverted to breaking stock that goes through the proper channels, or dumped — not sold as table eggs.
+
+Practically: the last dose lands five days from the start, so I'd keep House 5 eggs off the table market until five days after that — call it about ten days of House 5 volume in total, held back. I know that volume is real money and Brett won't love losing it, but selling through the withdrawal isn't something I can put my name to.
+
+Let me know you've got the egg side of the withdrawal handled and I'll note it in the treatment record.
+
+Karen Holzmann, DVM
+Prairie Avian Health
+PAH-2025-148
